@doc """
One step of a response, as `Response.Parser.next` returns it.

`Response` carries the head of a response, with an empty body. `Data`
carries body bytes. `End` says that the response is complete.

A 1xx response other than 101 is an interim response. It comes as a
`Response` with no `End`, and the `Response` of the final response
follows it.
"""
enum Response.Parser.Event
  Data(Binary)
  End
  Response(Response)
end
